17.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -128.64 19.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="9.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch6.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch6.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The Null Tower (<math id="Ch6.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>) structure in the epistemic vacuum (<math id="Ch6.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>) within semantic state space (<math id="Ch6.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch6.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Null Tower models the agent’s cognitive genesis not as a random accumulation of facts, but as a structured ascent. Beginning with minimal, unstructured semantic states, belief states are iteratively constructed via abstraction operators that impose layers of semantic organization. The resulting tower encodes the origin, trajectory, and coherence of the agent’s thought, providing a dynamic scaffold built entirely through the process of recursive generalization. It offers a generative account of how belief systems, planning structures, and even self-models can arise from a state of epistemic nullity, grounding the agent’s cognitive architecture in a minimal, introspectively accessible foundation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch6.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6.2. </span>Preliminaries: Vacuum, Layers, and Abstraction</h4>

<div id="Ch6.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before constructing the tower, we revisit key concepts. The epistemic vacuum <math id="Ch6.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subset\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subset\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of semantically inert belief states, or null states. Within this vacuum, we identify a foundational layer:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch6.S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Irreducible Null Stratum):</span> The irreducible null stratum <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> containing null states that have not themselves been produced by an abstraction process operating within <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(0)}=\Omega\setminus\Lambda(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(0)}=\Omega\setminus\Lambda(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is the abstraction operator (defined below). Elements <math id="Ch6.S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> serve as the ultimate seeds or origins for cognitive structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The construction relies on the concept of semantic layers or scales <math id="Ch6.S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="Ch6.S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> representing increasing levels of abstraction or generality (previewed in Chapter <a href="#Ch5" title="Chapter 5 The Semantic State Space ‣ Part II Semantic Foundations: The Semantic Substrate ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and detailed in Chapter <a href="#Ch10" title="Chapter 10 Semantic Scaling ‣ Part III Structuring Belief: Modularity and Abstraction ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). Transitions between these layers are mediated by abstraction operators:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch6.S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Abstraction Operator):</span> The abstraction operator <math id="Ch6.S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda:\Phi^{(k)}\rightarrow\Phi^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda:\Phi^{(k)}\rightarrow\Phi^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> maps a belief state <math id="Ch6.S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> at abstraction level k to a more abstract (e.g., compressed, generalized) belief state <math id="Ch6.S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> at level <math id="Ch6.S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the k-fold composition of abstraction as <math id="Ch6.S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{k}=\Lambda\circ\dots\circ\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{k}=\Lambda\circ\dots\circ\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (composition <math id="Ch6.S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> times, with <math id="Ch6.S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> being the identity). These operators are the engines driving the construction of the Null Tower.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch6.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6.3. </span>Tower Construction from the Epistemic Vacuum</h4>

<div id="Ch6.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Null Tower is constructed recursively for each irreducible null state <math id="Ch6.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch6.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch6.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="278.52" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 150.19 278.52" width="150.19"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,278.52) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(100.7,0) translate(0,16.02)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -49.21 -15.75 h 98.43 v 31.5 h -98.43 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.06 -5.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.54em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.05em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="58.12"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(0)}\in\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(0)}\in\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -49.21 43.31 h 98.43 v 31.5 h -98.43 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.55 54.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.02em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="14.94" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="77.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(1)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(1)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -49.21 102.36 h 98.43 v 31.5 h -98.43 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.55 113.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.02em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="14.94" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="77.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(2)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(2)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(1)})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -49.21 161.42 h 98.43 v 31.5 h -98.43 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.55 172.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.02em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="14.94" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="77.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(3)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(3)}=\Lambda(\omega^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.8pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 196.85 L 0 230.26"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 227.09)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.85 246.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.83" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="27.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(\infty)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(\infty)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 16.02 L 0 38.65"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 36.39)"><path d="M 5.9 0 L 0.89 1.87 L 2.4 0 L 0.89 -1.87 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 75.08 L 0 97.7"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 95.44)"><path d="M 5.9 0 L 0.89 1.87 L 2.4 0 L 0.89 -1.87 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 134.14 L 0 156.76"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 154.5)"><path d="M 5.9 0 L 0.89 1.87 L 2.4 0 L 0.89 -1.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -87.44 61.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.31em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="106.41"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch6.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Abstraction depth <math id="Ch6.F2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch6.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6.2</span>. </span><span id="Ch6.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Recursive construction of the Null Tower. Starting from an irreducible null state <math id="Ch6.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(0)}\in\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(0)}\in\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, successive applications of the abstraction operator <math id="Ch6.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> generate higher null states <math id="Ch6.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, converging toward the semantic singularity <math id="Ch6.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(\infty)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(\infty)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch6.S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch6.S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Recursive Abstraction):</span> Given <math id="Ch6.S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, its level-k abstraction <math id="Ch6.S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="Ch6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(k)}:=\Lambda^{k}(\omega)\quad\text{for }k\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(k)}:=\Lambda^{k}(\omega)\quad\text{for }k\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch6.S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="Ch6.S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{(k)}\in\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{(k)}\in\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a semantic structure of abstraction depth k, inheriting compressed or reorganized content from the layers below. The sequence <math id="Ch6.S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\omega^{(0)},\omega^{(1)},\omega^{(2)},\ldots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\omega^{(0)},\omega^{(1)},\omega^{(2)},\ldots\}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a specific belief trajectory originating from <math id="Ch6.S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This process allows us to define the layers of the Null Tower itself:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch6.S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch6.S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch6.S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Null Tower Layers):</span> The k-th layer of the Null Tower, <math id="Ch6.S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the set of all belief states reachable by applying exactly k levels of abstraction to the irreducible null stratum:</p>
<table id="Ch6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(k)}:=\Lambda^{k}(\Omega^{(0)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(k)}:=\Lambda^{k}(\Omega^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch6.S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">These layers form a stratification of the null-derived belief space: <math id="Ch6.S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{k=0}^{\infty}\Omega^{(k)}\subseteq\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{k=0}^{\infty}\Omega^{(k)}\subseteq\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> strictly reachable from the base of the Null Tower, the irreducible null stratum <math id="Ch6.S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every belief state constructed purely by abstraction from <math id="Ch6.S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to a unique layer k.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch6.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch6.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="369.95" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 371.89 369.95" width="371.89"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,369.95) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(163.85,0) translate(0,52.71)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 189.9 -36.17"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.98235 -0.1871 0.1871 0.98235 190.44 -36.27)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 194.19 -48.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="9.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch6.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 189.99 93.06"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.89806 0.43987 -0.43987 0.89806 190.49 93.3)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 297.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset=