0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{4}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 140.18 100.81 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 145.65 112.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{4}^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{4}^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 140.18 140.18 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 145.65 152.26)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{4}^{(4)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{4}^{(4)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 140.18 179.55 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 145.65 191.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{4}^{(5)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{4}^{(5)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 -17.3 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 -5.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 22.07 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 34.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 61.44 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 73.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 100.81 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 112.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 140.18 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 152.26)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(4)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(4)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.55 179.55 h 34.59 v 34.59 h -34.59 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 185.02 191.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.92em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="13.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.83)" width="23.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F1.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{5}^{(5)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{5}^{(5)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch12.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch12.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic geometry grid illustrating the belief space <math id="Ch12.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> as a 2D structure indexed by semantic sector <math id="Ch12.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and abstraction level <math id="Ch12.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Each cell <math id="Ch12.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> contains beliefs of a specific type and resolution. A belief state <math id="Ch12.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> can span multiple cells. Arrows indicate epistemic transitions via abstraction and sectoral translation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch12.S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A typical belief state <math id="Ch12.S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is not confined to a single cell but exists as an ensemble distributed across a region of this manifold:</p>
<table id="Ch12.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch12.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\bigcup_{(\Sigma,k)}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma},\quad\text{where }\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}=\phi\cap\Sigma^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\bigcup_{(\Sigma,k)}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma},\quad\text{where }\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}=\phi\cap\Sigma^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch12.S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This allows agents to hold mixed-resolution beliefs simultaneously (e.g., detailed perception <math id="Ch12.S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{(0)}_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{(0)}_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math> alongside abstract goals <math id="Ch12.S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{(2)}_{plan}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{(2)}_{plan}</annotation></semantics></math>). The structure supports a notion of local topology. Adjacent cells are connected by specific operators:</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vertical connections:</span> Between <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k+1)</annotation></semantics></math> via abstraction/elaboration operators <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda|_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda|_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V|_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V|_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Horizontal connections:</span> Between <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma_{i},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma_{i},k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma_{j},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma_{j},k)</annotation></semantics></math> via sector translation or projection operators <math id="Ch12.S2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\Sigma_{i}\rightarrow\Sigma_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\Sigma_{i}\rightarrow\Sigma_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diagonal connections:</span> Represent composite operations involving both scaling and sectoral shifts.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch12.S2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">These transitions define the fundamental geometry of epistemic change within <math id="Ch12.S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch12.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch12.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="258.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 280.69 258.79" width="280.69"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,258.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(8.13,0) translate(0,8.87)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 247.58 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 244.41 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 258.71 -4.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="9.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 225.54"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 222.36)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.51 236.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="7.03"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 0 L 55.12 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 110.24 0 L 110.24 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 165.35 0 L 165.35 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 220.47 0 L 220.47 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 55.12 L 242.52 55.12"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 110.24 L 242.52 110.24"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 165.35 L 242.52 165.35"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 44.09 22.05 C 69.99 47.94 74.17 81.83 110.24 88.19 C 137.44 92.99 138.15 127.49 165.35 132.28 C 192.75 137.11 191.03 174.54 213.27 185.13"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.95193 0.3063 -0.3063 0.95193 209.41 183.84)"><path d="M 9.41 0 L 2.68 2.49 L 4.5 0 L 2.68 -2.49 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 25.57 8.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="13.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 159.12 139.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="12.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 225.36 195.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="14.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch12.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12.2</span>. </span><span id="Ch12.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A semantic trajectory representing the evolution of a belief state <math id="Ch12.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> over time in the <math id="Ch12.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> plane. The trajectory reflects both abstraction (increasing <math id="Ch12.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) and sectoral shifts (along <math id="Ch12.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.3. </span>Semantic Coordinates and Belief Positioning</h4>

<div id="Ch12.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each belief component <math id="Ch12.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> within an ensemble <math id="Ch12.S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> can be assigned conceptual semantic coordinates <math id="Ch12.S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> indicating its primary sector and abstraction level.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Coordinate Map):</span> We can define a (potentially context-dependent) map <math id="Ch12.S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi:\Phi\rightarrow\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{S}\times\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi:\Phi\rightarrow\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{S}\times\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0})</annotation></semantics></math> that assigns a set of coordinates to a belief state or its components. For simplicity, we often refer to the primary coordinate <math id="Ch12.S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ch12.S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\subseteq\Sigma^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\subseteq\Sigma^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> or where the "center of mass" lies.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Given a belief ensemble <math id="Ch12.S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> distributed across the manifold, we can define projections:</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sectoral Projection:</span> <math id="Ch12.S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\Sigma}(\phi)=\phi\cap\Sigma=\bigcup_{k}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\Sigma}(\phi)=\phi\cap\Sigma=\bigcup_{k}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> (isolates content within a specific sector).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scale Projection:</span> <math id="Ch12.S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}(\phi)=\phi\cap\Phi^{(k)}=\bigcup_{\Sigma}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}(\phi)=\phi\cap\Phi^{(k)}=\bigcup_{\Sigma}\phi^{(k)}_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> (isolates content at a specific abstraction level).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch12.S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The distribution of belief across the grid <math id="Ch12.S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math>, as visualized conceptually in the diagram above, can be quantified by a belief density or activation function <math id="Ch12.S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\Sigma^{(k)},\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\Sigma^{(k)},\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can also define an epistemic center of mass CoM<math id="Ch12.S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> using this density, providing a single (though potentially crude) indicator of the agent’s current semantic focus within the 2D space. The dynamic evolution of this center tracks shifts in cognitive focus (e.g., from perception to reflection).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.4. </span>Operators as Trajectories in <math id="Ch12.S4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="Ch12.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within the semantic geometry framework, epistemic operations are interpreted as movements or transformations generating trajectories across the manifold <math id="Ch12.S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Atomic Epistemic Motions):</span> Given a belief <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\Sigma^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\Sigma^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, primitive operations induce motion in the conceptual (<math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, k) space:</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upward Abstraction (<math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>): Vertical movement to <math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Downward Elaboration (<math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>): Vertical movement to <math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sectoral Translation (<math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\Sigma\rightarrow\Sigma^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\Sigma\rightarrow\Sigma^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>): Horizontal movement to <math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma^{\prime},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma^{\prime},k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assimilation (<math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(k)}_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(k)}_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>): Injection of new content at coordinate <math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Nullification/Annihilation (<math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t},K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t},K</annotation></semantics></math>): Decay or removal of content, potentially moving towards the epistemic vacuum <math id="Ch12.S4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> (the origin/boundary).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch12.S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Complex cognitive processes correspond to composite trajectories, sequences of these atomic motions. Let <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:[t_{0},t_{1}]\rightarrow\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:[t_{0},t_{1}]\rightarrow\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be an epistemic trajectory. It can be decomposed as <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\gamma_{n}\circ\dots\circ\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\gamma_{n}\circ\dots\circ\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a transformation induced by an operator (<math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda,V,T,A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda,V,T,A</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.). For example, processing an observation might involve a trajectory starting in <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{(0)}_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{(0)}_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math>, moving via abstraction to <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{(1)}_{narr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{(1)}_{narr}</annotation></semantics></math>, then perhaps via reflection into <math id="Ch12.S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{(2)}_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{(2)}_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This perspective allows us to model cognitive control using trajectory fields <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\Phi\rightarrow T\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\Phi\rightarrow T\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the tangent bundle of <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. The evolution of belief follows <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\gamma}{dt}=F(\gamma(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\gamma}{dt}=F(\gamma(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. Meta-control policies <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{meta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{meta}</annotation></semantics></math> can then be framed as selecting fields or guiding trajectories towards target regions <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\subset\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\subset\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Importantly, due to the non-invertibility of <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, epistemic trajectories often exhibit path-dependence or hysteresis: the state <math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t)</annotation></semantics></math> depends not only on its current coordinates but also on the path taken to reach them (<math id="Ch12.S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\circ\Lambda\neq\text{id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mtext>id</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\circ\Lambda\neq\text{id}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S5" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.5. </span>Metric Structure and Semantic Distance (Preview)</h4>

<div id="Ch12.S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To fully leverage the geometric interpretation, <math id="Ch12.S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> should ideally be endowed with a notion of distance. We postulate a semantic distance function <math id="Ch12.S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d:\Phi\times\Phi\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d:\Phi\times\Phi\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying standard metric axioms (non-negativity, identity of indiscernibles, symmetry, triangle inequality). This metric quantifies the "semantic difference" between belief states. (The formal construction and learning of such metrics are discussed further in Part <a href="#Pt9" title="Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a>, Chapter <a href="#Ch34" title="Chapter 34 Learning Semantic Structures ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conceptually, this distance might be decomposable:</p>
<table id="Ch12.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch12.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\approx\alpha\cdot d_{sector}(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})+\beta\cdot d_{scale}(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\approx\alpha\cdot d_{sector}(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})+\beta\cdot d_{scale}(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch12.S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch12.S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{sector}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{sector}</annotation></semantics></math> measures distance across functional modalities and <math id="Ch12.S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{scale}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{scale}</annotation></semantics></math> measures distance across abstraction levels, weighted by <math id="Ch12.S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Such a metric, <span id="Ch12.S5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while potentially challenging to define precisely and learn effectively</span>, enables:</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coherence Measurement:</span> Quantifying the divergence between related beliefs (e.g., <math id="Ch12.S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\phi^{(k)},\Lambda(\phi^{(k-1)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\phi^{(k)},\Lambda(\phi^{(k-1)}))</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability Diagnostics:</span> Tracking semantic drift <math id="Ch12.S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\phi_{0},\phi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\phi_{0},\phi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> over time.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Neighborhood Definition:</span> Defining local regions <math id="Ch12.S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\epsilon}(\phi)=\{\phi^{\prime}|d(\phi,\phi^{\prime})&lt;\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\epsilon}(\phi)=\{\phi^{\prime}|d(\phi,\phi^{\prime})&lt;\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math> for local updates or attention.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cost of Thought:</span> Potentially defining trajectory curvature or transformation cost based on distance travelled vs. displacement.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch12.S5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The metric structure turns <math id="Ch12.S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> from a simple grid into a space where proximity implies semantic similarity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.6. </span>Cognitive Dynamics and Semantic Flow</h4>

<div id="Ch12.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evolution of belief <math id="Ch12.S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t)</annotation></semantics></math> within the semantic geometry can be modeled as a semantic flow governed by internal and external forces acting on the belief state.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition (Epistemic Vector Fields):</span> We can conceptually define vector fields <math id="Ch12.S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\Phi\rightarrow T\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\Phi\rightarrow T\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> that assign a direction and magnitude of change <math id="Ch12.S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> to each belief state <math id="Ch12.S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. The belief trajectory <math id="Ch12.S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> follows <math id="Ch12.S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\gamma}{dt}=F(\gamma(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\gamma}{dt}=F(\gamma(t))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note on Practicality:</span> Defining and computing such a field <math id="Ch12.S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> across the entirety of the high-dimensional space <math id="Ch12.S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is highly complex and likely requires significant abstraction or approximation in practice. However, the concept is useful for modeling cognitive tendencies:</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An abstraction flow pushing beliefs vertically towards higher <math id="Ch12.S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A grounding flow pulling beliefs towards lower <math id="Ch12.S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch12.S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attractor dynamics where flows converge towards stable fixed points <math id="Ch12.S6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., coherent schemas, reflective equilibria) where <math id="Ch12.S6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\phi^{*})\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\phi^{*})\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Repeller dynamics where flows diverge from unstable regions (e.g., areas of high contradiction).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Ch12.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch12.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="258.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 280.69 258.79" width="280.69"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,258.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(8.13,0) translate(0,8.87)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 247.58 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 244.41 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 258.71 -4.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="9.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 225.54"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 222.36)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.51 236.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="7.03"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 0 L 55.12 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 110.24 0 L 110.24 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 165.35 0 L 165.35 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 220.47 0 L 220.47 220.47"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 55.12 L 242.52 55.12"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 110.24 L 242.52 110.24"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 165.35 L 242.52 165.35"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 55.12 L 73.86 83.23"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.55469 0.83206 -0.83206 0.55469 72.1 80.59)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 110.24 55.12 L 123.19 72.4"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.59999 0.8 -0.8 0.59999 121.29 69.86)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 165.35 55.12 L 173.71 71.83"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.44724 0.89441 -0.89441 0.44724 172.29 69)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 110.24 L 61.93 117.05"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.7071 0.7071 -0.7071 0.7071 59.68 114.8)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 110.24 110.24 L 118.59 126.95"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.44724 0.89441 -0.89441 0.44724 117.18 124.12)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 165.35 110.24 L 165.35 137.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 165.35 134.18)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 165.35 L 60.18 165.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 57.01 165.35)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 110.24 165.35 L 126.95 173.71"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.89441 0.44724 -0.44724 0.89441 124.12 172.29)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 165.35 165.35 L 172.16 172.16"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.7071 0.7071 -0.7071 0.7071 169.92 169.92)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><path d="M 198.43 198.43 M 200.63 198.43 C 200.63 199.64 199.64 200.63 198.43 200.63 C 197.21 200.63 196.22 199.64 196.22 198.43 C 196.22 197.21 197.21 196.22 198.43 196.22 C 199.64 196.22 200.63 197.21 200.63 198.43 Z M 198.43 198.43"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 203.31 203.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.66)" width="49.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F3.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">attractor</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.12 55.12 M 59.53 55.12 C 59.53 57.55 57.55 59.53 55.12 59.53 C 52.68 59.53 50.71 57.55 50.71 55.12 C 50.71 52.68 52.68 50.71 55.12 50.71 C 57.55 50.71 59.53 52.68 59.53 55.12 Z M 55.12 55.12"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.56 41.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="41.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F3.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">repeller</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch12.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12.3</span>. </span><span id="Ch12.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic flow field <math id="Ch12.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> over the <math id="Ch12.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> plane. Arrows represent preferred semantic transitions. Certain regions act as attractors (stable belief configurations), while others serve as repellers (unstable or disorganized states).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch12.S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These flows can be influenced by assimilation (injecting momentum), nullification (a general drift towards <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>), anchoring (creating stable points), and control policies (actively shaping the effective field <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>). Concepts like semantic drift can be detected by monitoring deviation from expected flow lines or stable regions. Feedback mechanisms can then adjust the effective flow field <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> to implement re-centering or correction. Meta-control becomes a problem of navigating or modulating these flows to achieve cognitive goals. Furthermore, stable cyclical flows passing through sequences of sectors and scales (e.g., perceive <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> narrate <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> plan <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> reflect <math id="Ch12.S6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> perceive) can model cognitive rhythms or standard operational loops.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S7" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.7. </span>Visualization and Diagrammatic Models</h4>

<div id="Ch12.S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The power of semantic geometry lies partly in its potential for visualization, providing intuitive "cognitive maps" (like the conceptual grid diagram introduced earlier).</p>
<ul id="Ch12.S7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Semantic Grid (Sector <math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> Scale):</span> The primary visualization plots semantic sectors (<math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) along one axis (e.g., horizontal) and abstraction level (<math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) along the other (e.g., vertical). Belief states <math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> or their components are represented as points, regions, or density distributions on this grid.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trajectory Arrows:</span> Paths traced on the grid show epistemic evolution. Vertical arrows denote scaling (<math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda,V</annotation></semantics></math>), horizontal arrows denote sectoral shifts (<math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>), and diagonal arrows represent combined operations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Flow Fields:</span> Vector arrows overlaid on the grid can illustrate the direction and magnitude of typical belief motion (<math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>) in different regions. Attractors and repellers become visually apparent.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Belief Density Heatmaps:</span> Coloring grid cells <math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> based on belief activation or mass <math id="Ch12.S7.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\Sigma^{(k)},\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\Sigma^{(k)},\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> shows the agent’s current semantic focus and the distribution of its cognitive load.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch12.S7.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch12.S7.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch12.S7.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cycle Diagrams:</span> Closed loops on the grid can represent recurring cognitive processes or operational cycles (e.g., sense-plan-act loop).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Ch12.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch12.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="259" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 399.37 259" width="399.37"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,259) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(138.35,0) translate(0,98.98)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -137.8 0 L 136.69 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 137.24 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 142.96 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="113.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (Semantic Sector)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -98.43 L 0 136.69"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 137.24)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -60.36 146.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="121.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (Abstraction Level)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 96.93 17.09 L 95.63 23.28 L 93.94 29.38 L 91.86 35.36 L 89.39 41.19 L 86.56 46.85 L 83.37 52.31 L 79.84 57.56 L 75.98 62.57 L 71.8 67.32 L 67.32 71.8 L 62.57 75.98 L 57.56 79.84 L 52.31 83.37 L 46.85 86.56 L 41.19 89.39 L 35.36 91.86 L 29.38 93.94 L 23.28 95.63 L 22.93 95.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.97871 0.20525 -0.20525 -0.97871 26.03 95.06)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -17.09 96.93 L -23.28 95.63 L -29.38 93.94 L -35.36 91.86 L -41.19 89.39 L -46.85 86.56 L -52.31 83.37 L -57.56 79.84 L -62.57 75.98 L -67.32 71.8 L -71.8 67.32 L -75.98 62.57 L -79.84 57.56 L -83.37 52.31 L -86.56 46.85 L -89.39 41.19 L -91.86 35.36 L -93.94 29.38 L -95.63 23.28 L -95.71 22.93"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.20525 -0.97871 0.97871 -0.20525 -95.06 26.03)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -96.93 -17.09 L -95.63 -23.28 L -93.94 -29.38 L -91.86 -35.36 L -89.39 -41.19 L -86.56 -46.85 L -83.37 -52.31 L -79.84 -57.56 L -75.98 -62.57 L -71.8 -67.32 L -67.32 -71.8 L -62.57 -75.98 L -57.56 -79.84 L -52.31 -83.37 L -46.85 -86.56 L -41.19 -89.39 L -35.36 -91.86 L -29.38 -93.94 L -23.28 -95.63 L -22.93 -95.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.97871 -0.20525 0.20525 0.97871 -26.03 -95.06)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 17.09 -96.93 L 23.28 -95.63 L 29.38 -93.94 L 35.36 -91.86 L 41.19 -89.39 L 46.85 -86.56 L 52.31 -83.37 L 57.56 -79.84 L 62.57 -75.98 L 67.32 -71.8 L 71.8 -67.32 L 75.98 -62.57 L 79.84 -57.56 L 83.37 -52.31 L 86.56 -46.85 L 89.39 -41.19 L 91.86 -35.36 L 93.94 -29.38 L 95.63 -23.28 L 95.71 -22.93"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.20525 0.97871 -0.97871 0.20525 95.06 -26.03)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 27.74 51.44 h 86.25 v 15.22 h -86.25 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 30.51 56.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="72.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Assimilation (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -108.81 51.44 h 83.76 v 15.22 h -83.76 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -106.04 56.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="69.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Elaboration (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -108.37 -66.67 h 82.89 v 15.22 h -82.89 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -105.61 -61.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="69.33"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Sector Shift (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 31.9 -66.67 h 77.94 v 15.22 h -77.94 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.66 -61.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.51em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="60.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Reflection (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 37.58 -7.61 h 82.31 v 15.22 h -82.31 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 40.35 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="69.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Abstraction (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -124.05 -7.61 h 90.61 v 15.22 h -90.61 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -121.28 -2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.54em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="72.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch12.F4.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Nullification (<math id="Ch12.F4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch12.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12.4</span>. </span><span id="Ch12.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic epistemic cycle represented as a closed process loop in the <math id="Ch12.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math> plane. The cycle flows through assimilation (<math id="Ch12.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>) of new information, elaboration (<math id="Ch12.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>) for grounded realization, nullification (<math id="Ch12.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) for cleanup, sectoral translation (<math id="Ch12.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) across functional modalities, reflection (<math id="Ch12.F4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>) for evaluation, and abstraction (<math id="Ch12.F4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) to higher levels, enabling continual evolution of the belief state within the structured semantic manifold.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch12.S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These diagrams transform the abstract structure of <math id="Ch12.S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> into an interpretable map, aiding design, debugging, introspection, and theoretical understanding.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch12.S8" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">12.8. </span>Conclusion: Belief as Navigation</h4>

<div id="Ch12.S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic geometry provides a unified framework for structuring the belief space <math id="Ch12.S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> by integrating the functional modularity of semantic sectors (<math id="Ch12.S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>) with the hierarchical depth of semantic scaling (<math id="Ch12.S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>). This construes <math id="Ch12.S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> as a conceptual two-dimensional epistemic manifold where beliefs are positioned by coordinates <math id="Ch12.S8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Within this geometry, epistemic operations manifest as structured trajectories, semantic distance provides a measure of coherence and change (though defining it precisely is challenging), and belief evolution can be modeled as dynamic flows governed by vector fields (a complex theoretical ideal). Visualization tools based on this geometry offer intuitive maps of cognitive states and processes.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch12.S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Ultimately, semantic geometry reframes cognition: to think is to move within a structured landscape of meaning. By endowing <math id="Ch12.S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> with this structure, we provide agents with an internal map and compass, enabling more organized reasoning, targeted control, and navigable introspection. It provides the spatial logic for how belief states relate, transform, and guide behavior.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch12.S8.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Chapter Summary</h5>

<div id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter introduces Semantic Geometry, unifying the concepts of Semantic Scaling (abstraction levels <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>) and Semantic Sectors (functional modules <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>) into a cohesive geometric framework for the belief space <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It conceptualizes <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> as a structured manifold where belief states (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>) can be positioned using coordinates <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,k)</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting both functional role and abstraction level. Cognitive dynamics, driven by operators like Assimilation (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>), Abstraction (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), Elaboration (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>), Nullification (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), and Annihilation (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>), are interpreted as generating structured trajectories (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>) across this manifold. The chapter discusses the concept of an underlying epistemic flow field (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>) governing these trajectories and postulates the existence of a semantic distance metric (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>) to quantify belief similarity and coherence (<math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>). This geometric perspective allows for intuitive visualizations (e.g., the <math id="Ch12.S8.SSx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\times k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\times k</annotation></semantics></math> grid) and reframes cognitive processes, including regulation and control, as forms of navigation within a structured internal landscape of meaning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt4" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_part">Part IV </span>Epistemic Dynamics: Evolution of Thought</h2>

<section id="Ch13" class="ltx_chapter">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 13 </span>Assimilation</h3>

<section id="Ch13.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">13.1. </span>Introduction: Integrating New Information</h4>

<div id="Ch13.S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Having established the foundational structures of the semantic state space <math id="Ch13.S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> (potentially parameterized as <math id="Ch13.S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{[\theta]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{[\theta]}</annotation></semantics></math>, Chapter <a href="#Ch8" title="Chapter 8 Parameterized Semantic Architectures ‣ Part II Semantic Foundations: The Semantic Substrate ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), the Null Tower (Chapter <a href="#Ch6" title="Chapter 6 The Null Tower ‣ Part II Semantic Foundations: The Semantic Substrate ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), belief construction (Chapter <a href="#Ch7" title="Chapter 7 Belief Construction ‣ Part II Semantic Foundations: The Semantic Substrate ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and the organizing principles of semantic scaling and sectors (Part <a href="#Pt3" title="Part III Structuring Belief: Modularity and Abstraction ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>), we now turn to the core dynamics that govern how belief states <math id="Ch13.S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> evolve over time. The most fundamental process driving belief change in response to interaction or internal generation is assimilation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch13.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assimilation is the mechanism by which an agent integrates new, structured, object-level input derived from observations, communication, or certain internal processes like simulation, into its existing belief ensemble <math id="Ch13.S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It is the primary way an agent learns from experience, adapts its understanding, and extends its knowledge base regarding the world or hypothetical scenarios. We formalize this process via the assimilation operator:</p>
<table id="Ch13.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch13.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:\Phi\times\Phi_{input}\rightarrow\Phi" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:\Phi\times\Phi_{input}\rightarrow\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch13.S1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch13.S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{current}\in\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{current}\in\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the agent’s current belief state, <math id="Ch13.S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> is the structured representation of the new object-level information (e.g., output of the observation encoder, <math id="Ch13.S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}=X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}=X(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, or result of a simulation), and <math id="Ch13.S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{new}=A(\phi_{current},\phi_{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{new}=A(\phi_{current},\phi_{input})</annotation></semantics></math> is the resulting updated belief state.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch13.S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, assimilation is not mere accumulation or concatenation. It is an active, context-sensitive, and structure-preserving process. It must determine how the new information relates to existing beliefs, handle potential conflicts, update relevant structures, potentially trigger further inferences or elaborations, and maintain the overall coherence (<math id="Ch13.S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) of the agent’s epistemic state. Assimilation bridges the gap between perception/input and sustained, structured belief, forming the constructive engine of epistemic evolution for object-level knowledge. (Note: The integration of internally generated meta-cognitive or introspective insights is handled by the distinct Meta-Assimilation operator <math id="Ch13.S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, detailed in Chapter <a href="#Ch28" title="Chapter 28 Meta-Assimilation: Integrating Introspective Beliefs ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch13.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">13.2. </span>Philosophical and Cognitive Motivations</h4>

<div id="Ch13.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The nature of the assimilation operator <math id="Ch13.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is informed by core principles of cognition and epistemology. As discussed in Chapter <a href="#Ch3" title="Chapter 3 Psychological Motivations ‣ Part I Context and Foundations ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> regarding initial construction, constructivist theories emphasize that knowledge is actively built, not passively received; new input <math id="Ch13.S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is interpreted through the lens of the existing state <math id="Ch13.S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Cognitive psychology highlights the role of schemas or mental models (<math id="Ch13.S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx\phi</annotation></semantics></math>) in organizing knowledge and guiding the integration of new information.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch13.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, human cognition strives for coherence, preferentially integrating information that aligns with existing beliefs and resisting or revising information that conflicts. Assimilation must reflect this bias, often reinforcing existing structures and establishing stable anchor points (<math id="Ch13.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>). However, when faced with significant conflict or surprise, assimilation must also be capable of triggering belief revision or schema accommodation. Finally, cognitive systems exhibit selective attention; assimilation is not expected to incorporate all aspects of input equally but should filter for salience and relevance relative to the current state and the agent’s goals. These principles motivate the formal desiderata for the operator <math id="Ch13.S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch13.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">13.3. </span>Formal Desiderata for Assimilation</h4>

<div id="Ch13.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A cognitively plausible assimilation operator <math id="Ch13.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\phi,\phi_{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\phi,\phi_{input})</annotation></semantics></math> should satisfy several key properties or desiderata:</p>
<dl id="Ch13.S3.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D1: Semantic Integration: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting state <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{new}</annotation></semantics></math> must meaningfully incorporate content derived from <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>, interpreted or modified in the context of <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It’s not just <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\cup\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\cup\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D2: Coherence Preservation: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> should typically maintain or increase the internal coherence <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> of the belief state. Significant drops in coherence should only occur if <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly triggers a revision process due to conflict.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D3: Salience Filtering: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> should operate selectively, prioritizing the integration of salient, relevant, or high-impact components of <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> over irrelevant details. Notionally, <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\phi,\phi_{input})=A(\phi,F(\phi_{input}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\phi,\phi_{input})=A(\phi,F(\phi_{input}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a salience filter.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D4: Revision Under Conflict: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> contradicts strongly held or coherent parts of <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> should include a mechanism for belief revision, potentially removing or modifying parts of <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> before integrating the new content. Notionally, <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\phi,\phi_{input})=(\phi\setminus R_{\text{rev}}(\phi,\phi_{input}))\cup\phi^{\prime}_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>rev</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\phi,\phi_{input})=(\phi\setminus R_{\text{rev}}(\phi,\phi_{input}))\cup\phi^{\prime}_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D5: Idempotence on Redundancy: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assimilating semantically redundant information (already present or implied in <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>) should result in minimal change to <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\phi,\phi_{input})\approx\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\phi,\phi_{input})\approx\phi</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> is redundant w.r.t. <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D6: Anchoring: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assimilation should contribute to the formation and strengthening of stable anchor points <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, reinforcing reliable beliefs and providing structure for future reasoning.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D7: Locality of Change: </span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the absence of major conflict, the primary modifications induced by <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> should be relatively localized within the structure of <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, affecting only the parts most relevant to <math id="Ch13.S3.I1.ix7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="Ch13.S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These desiderata guide the design of specific assimilation mechanisms, ensuring they produce belief updates that are robust, coherent, and adaptive.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch13.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch13.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="119.22" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 559.02 119.22" width="559.02"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,119.22) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(55.4,0) translate(0,99.26)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 49.58 19.69 L -49.58 19.69 C -52.64 19.69 -55.12 17.21 -55.12 14.15 L -55.12 -14.15 C -55.12 -17.21 -52.64 -19.69 -49.58 -19.69 L 49.58 -19.69 C 52.64 -19.69 55.12 -17.21 55.12 -14.15 L 55.12 14.15 C 55.12 17.21 52.64 19.69 49.58 19.69 Z M -55.12 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.37 -3.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="86.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Incoming Input</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 184 19.69 L 84.83 19.69 C 81.77 19.69 79.29 17.21 79.29 14.15 L 79.29 -14.15 C 79.29 -17.21 81.77 -19.69 84.83 -19.69 L 184 -19.69 C 187.05 -19.69 189.53 -17.21 189.53 -14.15 L 189.53 14.15 C 189.53 17.21 187.05 19.69 184 19.69 Z M 79.29 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 110.31 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="48.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Filtering</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 319.97 19.69 L 219.24 19.69 C 216.18 19.69 213.71 17.21 213.71 14.15 L 213.71 -14.15 C 213.71 -17.21 216.18 -19.69 219.24 -19.69 L 319.97 -19.69 C 323.03 -19.69 325.51 -17.21 325.51 -14.15 L 325.51 14.15 C 325.51 17.21 323.03 19.69 319.97 19.69 Z M 213.71 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 218.32 -4.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="102.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Conflict Detection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 485.25 19.69 L 355.22 19.69 C 352.16 19.69 349.68 17.21 349.68 14.15 L 349.68 -14.15 C 349.68 -17.21 352.16 -19.69 355.22 -19.69 L 485.25 -19.69 C 488.3 -19.69 490.78 -17.21 490.78 -14.15 L 490.78 14.15 C 490.78 17.21 488.3 19.69 485.25 19.69 Z M 349.68 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 354.3 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="132.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Revision &amp; Adjustment</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 497.82 -59.61 L 342.65 -59.61 C 339.59 -59.61 337.11 -62.09 337.11 -65.14 L 337.11 -93.44 C 337.11 -96.5 339.59 -98.98 342.65 -98.98 L 497.82 -98.98 C 500.87 -98.98 503.35 -96.5 503.35 -93.44 L 503.35 -65.14 C 503.35 -62.09 500.87 -59.61 497.82 -59.61 Z M 337.11 -98.98"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 341.73 -82.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="157.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Integration into Belief State</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 307.4 -59.61 L 166.58 -59.61 C 163.53 -59.61 161.05 -62.09 161.05 -65.14 L 161.05 -93.44 C 161.05 -96.5 163.53 -98.98 166.58 -98.98 L 307.4 -98.98 C 310.46 -98.98 312.94 -96.5 312.94 -93.44 L 312.94 -65.14 C 312.94 -62.09 310.46 -59.61 307.4 -59.61 Z M 161.05 -98.98"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 165.66 -82.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="142.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Elaboration &amp; Expansion</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 131.34 -59.61 L -1.19 -59.61 C -4.24 -59.61 -6.72 -62.09 -6.72 -65.14 L -6.72 -93.44 C -6.72 -96.5 -4.24 -98.98 -1.19 -98.98 L 131.34 -98.98 C 134.4 -98.98 136.87 -96.5 136.87 -93.44 L 136.87 -65.14 C 136.87 -62.09 134.4 -59.61 131.34 -59.61 Z M -6.72 -98.98"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.11 -83.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="134.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch13.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Assimilated Belief State</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.39 0 L 73.06 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 69.88 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 189.81 0 L 207.47 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 204.3 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 325.79 0 L 343.45 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 340.27 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 420.23 -19.96 L 420.23 -53.37"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 420.23 -50.2)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 336.84 -79.29 L 319.18 -79.29"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 322.35 -79.29)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 160.77 -79.29 L 143.11 -79.29"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 146.28 -79.29)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch13.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch13.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overall Assimilation Process: Multi-stage flow of the Assimilation operator <math id="Ch13.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, progressing from initial input through filtering, conflict detection, revision, integration, and elaboration to form an enriched belief state.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch13.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">13.4. </span>Taxonomy of Assimilation Operators</h4>

<div id="Ch13.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assimilation is multifaceted. Different situations call for different modes of integration for object-level information. We can classify assimilation operators <math id="Ch13.S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> based on several factors:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch13.S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Ch13.S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Source of Input (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> (Must be non-meta-cognitive)</p>
<ul id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math>: Input from perception (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is sensory).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{text}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{text}</annotation></semantics></math>: Input from linguistic communication.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i1.I0.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{sim}</annotation></semantics></math>: Input from internal object-level simulation or hypothesis generation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assimilation Mode (Primary Function):</span></p>
<ul id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Elaborative (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{elab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{elab}</annotation></semantics></math>): Enriches <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> by adding inferred consequences or contextual details related to <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Corrective (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{corr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{corr}</annotation></semantics></math>): Resolves conflicts between <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> via revision.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Confirmatory (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{conf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{conf}</annotation></semantics></math>): Strengthens existing beliefs in <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> that are consistent with <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math>, often increasing anchoring <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Abstracting (<math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{abs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{abs}</annotation></semantics></math>): Generalizes over <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> (perhaps in light of patterns in <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>) to form higher-level beliefs <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i2.I0.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Depth of Integration:</span></p>
<ul id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Surface-Level: Adds new expressions <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with minimal change to the existing structure of <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structural: Modifies relationships (links, weights) between expressions within <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Schema-Modifying: Causes significant reorganization of belief clusters or interpretive frames within <math id="Ch13.S4.I1.i3.I0.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
