0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="74.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch31.F2.pic1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">State Update</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 20.41)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="17.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch31.F2.pic1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(</span><math id="Ch31.F2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{new}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch31.F2.pic1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="Ch31.F2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{lower}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">lower</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{lower}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch31.F2.pic1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 35.06 97.87 L 62.08 82.27"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.86607 -0.4999 0.4999 0.86607 59.34 83.86)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 105.86 38.82 L 111.71 5.6"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.17374 -0.98479 0.98479 0.17374 111.16 8.72)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 46.87 -20.51 L -40.9 -20.51"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 -37.73 -20.51)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -112.75 -0.27 L -106.89 32.95"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.17374 0.98479 -0.98479 0.17374 -107.44 29.82)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -67.23 79.29 L -40.2 94.89"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.86607 0.4999 -0.4999 0.86607 -42.95 93.31)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch31.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 31.2</span>. </span><span id="Ch31.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Feedback loop for cognitive load regulation. Measured load triggers meta-introspective awareness, guiding management decisions that produce actions modifying the belief state, closing the regulatory loop.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch31.S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Effective load management involves dynamically balancing task demands with available cognitive capacity using these (and potentially other) strategies, guided by meta-cognitive self-assessment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch31.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">31.6. </span>Distinguishing Load from Effort</h4>

<div id="Ch31.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It remains crucial to distinguish cognitive load (<math id="Ch31.S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, often proxied by <math id="Ch31.S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) from semantic effort (<math id="Ch31.S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, discussed in Chapter <a href="#Ch32" title="Chapter 32 Semantic Effort ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>):</p>
<ul id="Ch31.S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cognitive Load (<math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Represents the <span id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">demand</span> imposed on the agent’s cognitive system by the current belief state <math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, its complexity, the ongoing dynamics, and the task requirements. It is a measure of how much processing is needed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Semantic Effort (<math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Represents the finite cognitive resource <span id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">actively allocated and expended</span> by the agent to meet those demands, perform operations (<math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,M,\Lambda,V,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,M,\Lambda,V,R</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.), maintain coherence (<math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>), or achieve goals. It is a measure of the processing intensity being applied, constrained by the agent’s total capacity (<math id="Ch31.S6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch31.S6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Load and effort are strongly related but distinct concepts. High load often necessitates allocating high effort to cope. However, an agent might face high load but allocate low effort (leading to performance failure) or apply high effort even when load is low (e.g., during intense reflection). Conversely, applying high effort can itself increase load by generating complex intermediate states. Understanding this distinction is key: load is the challenge presented to the system, while effort is the resource deployed by the system in response.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch31.S7" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">31.7. </span>Conclusion: Load as a Regulatory Signal</h4>

<div id="Ch31.S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cognitive load is an intrinsic aspect of any finite cognitive system. Within the semantic state space framework, load can be conceptualized not merely as external resource usage, but as arising from the complexity, coherence demands, and dynamic intensity associated with the agent’s belief state <math id="Ch31.S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and its evolution. Measuring or estimating load via properties like belief density (<math id="Ch31.S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), coherence strain (<math id="Ch31.S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>), sectoral activation (<math id="Ch31.S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\alpha}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\alpha}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>), and dynamic rates provides crucial information for self-regulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch31.S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">High cognitive load leads to predictable degradations in performance and coherence, potentially triggering simplifying dynamics (<math id="Ch31.S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t},\Lambda,K_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t},\Lambda,K_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>). An agent equipped with meta-introspection can become aware of its load levels and proactively employ management strategies—ranging from information pruning and abstraction to mode shifting and task rescheduling—to maintain effective operation. Cognitive load thus serves as a vital internal regulatory signal, mediating the interplay between task demands, processing capacity, and cognitive strategy, and informing the crucial allocation of semantic effort (<math id="Ch31.S7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>). Understanding and managing load is therefore essential for building robust, scalable, and truly adaptive semantic agents.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch31.S7.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Chapter Summary</h5>

<div id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter introduces Cognitive Load (L, often proxied by <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) as a measure of the demand placed on an agent’s finite processing resources by its current cognitive state and ongoing tasks within the semantic manifold <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Load is conceptualized as arising intrinsically from factors such as the complexity and size of the active belief state (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>), the distribution of activity across demanding semantic sectors (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>), the span of active abstraction levels (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>), the strain involved in maintaining coherence (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>), the intensity of current belief dynamics (e.g., rate of <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, complexity of <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>), and meta-cognitive overhead. Exceeding the agent’s processing capacity leads to consequences like performance degradation, coherence breakdown, and potential reliance on simplifying heuristics or dynamics (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t},\Lambda,K_{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t},\Lambda,K_{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>). Meta-cognitive awareness of load, achieved through introspection (monitoring <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda,\kappa," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda,\kappa,</annotation></semantics></math> etc.) and integrated via Meta-Assimilation (<math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>), allows the agent to employ proactive load management strategies, including information pruning, abstraction, mode shifting, and resource reallocation (effort <math id="Ch31.S7.SSx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>). Cognitive Load (demand) is explicitly distinguished from Semantic Effort (applied resources, Chapter <a href="#Ch32" title="Chapter 32 Semantic Effort ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), serving as a vital regulatory signal for adaptive cognition.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch32" class="ltx_chapter">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 32 </span>Semantic Effort</h3>

<section id="Ch32.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.1. </span>Introduction: The Cost and Exertion of Cognition</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding chapter explored cognitive load (<math id="Ch32.S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>), representing the demand placed on the agent’s processing resources by the complexity and dynamics of its belief state <math id="Ch32.S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. However, load only describes the demand; it does not fully capture the agent’s active response. Cognitive processes like deep reasoning, careful assimilation, sustained attention, or complex simulation require not just passive capacity, but the active direction and application of limited internal resources.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch32.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter introduces the concept of Semantic Effort, denoted <math id="Ch32.S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch32.S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Semantic effort refers to the cognitive resources <span id="Ch32.S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">actively deployed or exerted</span> by the agent towards specific internal processes operating within the semantic state space <math id="Ch32.S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. If cognitive load <math id="Ch32.S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the burden imposed by the state and task, semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the intensity of processing applied to manage that burden, maintain coherence, achieve goals, or perform internal operations. It represents the <span id="Ch32.S1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">controllable investment</span> of the agent’s finite cognitive capacity.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch32.S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Understanding semantic effort is crucial for modeling the resource limitations of thought, the link between exertion and processing quality, the mechanisms underlying concentration and fatigue, and how agents might choose to engage deeply or superficially with cognitive tasks. This chapter defines semantic effort, explores its representation, discusses its direct consequences on belief dynamics and performance, and contrasts it with cognitive load. The subsequent chapter (Chapter <a href="#Ch33" title="Chapter 33 Semantic Focus and Effort Allocation Policies ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) will delve into the complex mechanisms and policies governing how this effort is allocated and directed, relating it to concepts of focus and attention.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.2. </span>Defining and Representing Semantic Effort (<math id="Ch32.S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conceptualize semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> as a quantifiable internal resource that fuels cognitive operations.</p>
<ul id="Ch32.S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effort as a Resource:</span> We assume an agent possesses a total available pool of cognitive processing capacity or "effort capacity" at any given time, <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>. Semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> represents the rate or intensity at which these resources are currently being consumed or applied by active cognitive processes. This could be a scalar value representing overall exertion (<math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>) or potentially a vector <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{1},\dots,\epsilon_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{1},\dots,\epsilon_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> representing effort applied to different concurrent processes (e.g., <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{A},\epsilon_{M},\epsilon_{orient},\epsilon_{sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{A},\epsilon_{M},\epsilon_{orient},\epsilon_{sim}</annotation></semantics></math>) such that <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\epsilon_{i}\leq E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\epsilon_{i}\leq E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relation to Implementation:</span> While abstract, <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> could correspond in concrete implementations to measures like allocated computational cycles, energy consumption in neuromorphic systems, depth of search in planning algorithms, or number of generative steps in LLM-based operators. The key is that it represents a finite, consumable, and potentially controllable resource tied to processing intensity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Representation in <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> Through meta-introspection (Chapter <a href="#Ch29" title="Chapter 29 Meta-Introspection ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) and meta-assimilation (<math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, Chapter <a href="#Ch28" title="Chapter 28 Meta-Assimilation: Integrating Introspective Beliefs ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), the agent might represent its current effort level as meta-beliefs within <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>. Examples: "Current overall semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is high (estimated 0.8 <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>)" or "Effort allocated to coherence maintenance <math id="Ch32.S2.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimal."</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Ch32.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is thus modeled as a quantifiable, limited internal resource reflecting the intensity of active cognitive engagement, distinct from the passive demand represented by load <math id="Ch32.S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch32.S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.3. </span>Allocation of Effort (Preview)</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While this chapter focuses on the nature of the effort resource <math id="Ch32.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the crucial question of how this finite resource is strategically distributed across competing cognitive processes and targets within <math id="Ch32.S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is fundamental to executive control and attention. This involves complex allocation policies (<math id="Ch32.S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>) informed by goals, load, coherence, and other meta-cognitive assessments. These critical mechanisms of resource allocation, control, and their relation to semantic focus are deferred for detailed exploration in the next chapter (Chapter <a href="#Ch33" title="Chapter 33 Semantic Focus and Effort Allocation Policies ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.4. </span>Consequences of Effort Exertion Level</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The amount of semantic effort <math id="Ch32.S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> allocated to and consumed by a specific cognitive process directly influences its execution and impact:</p>
<ul id="Ch32.S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Processing Quality and Speed:</span> Increased effort <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{O}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to an operator <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> (like <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,M,\Lambda,V,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,M,\Lambda,V,R</annotation></semantics></math>) generally leads to improved performance characteristics, such as deeper analysis, more thorough search, higher fidelity simulation, more robust regulation, faster convergence, or generation of more detailed/coherent output. Conversely, low effort may lead to superficial processing or heuristic application.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Counteracting Nullification (<math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Sustained semantic effort directed towards maintaining specific beliefs <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or structures (e.g., active rehearsal or processing within <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>) can actively boost their anchoring <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or refresh their persistence <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, thus counteracting the passive decay modelled by <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Effort sustains information against forgetting.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource Depletion and Fatigue:</span> The total effort capacity <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite. Sustained high effort exertion (<math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\approx E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\approx E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>) depletes this underlying resource, potentially leading to a state of "cognitive fatigue" where <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> is temporarily reduced, forcing a subsequent reduction in applied effort <math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact on Cognitive Load (<math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Applying high effort can itself contribute to cognitive load. Intensive computations or simulations generate complex intermediate states that increase the demands (<math id="Ch32.S4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>) on the system, creating a feedback loop between effort and load.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch32.S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The level of semantic effort exerted thus fundamentally modulates the depth, effectiveness, and sustainability of cognitive operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S5" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.5. </span>Semantic Effort versus Cognitive Load</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As highlighted in Chapter <a href="#Ch31" title="Chapter 31 Cognitive Load ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, it is crucial to distinguish semantic effort (<math id="Ch32.S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) from cognitive load (<math id="Ch32.S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, often proxied by <math id="Ch32.S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ul id="Ch32.S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Load (<math id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> An assessment of the <span id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">demand</span> imposed by the current state <math id="Ch32.S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, dynamics, and task complexity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effort (<math id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The <span id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">resource actively allocated</span> by the agent to meet demands and perform operations, constrained by <math id="Ch32.S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Ch32.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch32.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="225.7" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 398.11 225.7" width="398.11"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,225.7) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(53.35,0) translate(0,10.15)"><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 228.68 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 224.6 0)"><path d="M 9.41 0 L 2.68 2.49 L 4.5 0 L 2.68 -2.49 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 241.66 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="90.13"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cognitive Load <math id="Ch32.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 189.31"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 185.23)"><path d="M 9.41 0 L 2.68 2.49 L 4.5 0 L 2.68 -2.49 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -48.74 202.29)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="92.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic Effort <math id="Ch32.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 118.11 0 L 118.11 196.85"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 98.43 L 236.22 98.43"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 15.18 162.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.51em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="4.8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.8)" width="87.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Deliberate Reflection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 137.28 163.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.51em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.8)" width="80.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Focused Processing</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.2 65.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.51em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.8)" width="79.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Relaxed Processing</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 130.34 65.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.51em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:6.81pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.8)" width="93.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Overload and Collapse</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.69 147.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.34em;font-size:10pt;" height="25.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="98.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:7.14em;">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.7.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">e.g., Reflective self-monitoring</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 137.8 152.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.54em;font-size:10pt;" height="41.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="98.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:7.14em;">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.8.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">e.g., Active planning under pressure</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 19.69 53.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.54em;font-size:10pt;" height="41.82" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="98.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.9" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:7.14em;">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.9.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">e.g., Mind wandering, simple tasks</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 137.8 52.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="23.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="98.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.10" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:7.14em;">
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.10.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch32.F1.pic1.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">e.g., Panic, failure to reason</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch32.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 32.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch32.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic Load vs. Semantic Effort space. Different regions illustrate how the agent’s performance varies depending on the relationship between cognitive load <math id="Ch32.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (demand) and semantic effort <math id="Ch32.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (applied resource).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch32.S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">They are coupled but distinct: high <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> often necessitates high <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, insufficient <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> relative to <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> leads to overload consequences (Section 3, Chapter <a href="#Ch31" title="Chapter 31 Cognitive Load ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), and high <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> can contribute to <math id="Ch32.S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Load is the challenge; effort is the applied (and limited) resource.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.6. </span>Control of Effort Allocation (Preview)</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The meta-cognitive processes that determine how much effort <math id="Ch32.S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to exert and where to direct it are central to strategic cognitive control. These control policies (<math id="Ch32.S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>) operate based on introspective assessments and goals, as will be detailed in Chapter <a href="#Ch33" title="Chapter 33 Semantic Focus and Effort Allocation Policies ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch32.S7" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">32.7. </span>Conclusion: Effort as the Currency of Cognition</h4>

<div id="Ch32.S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic effort, <math id="Ch32.S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, represents the active deployment of finite cognitive resources within the Semantic Manifold framework. It is the "currency" spent to perform demanding operations, maintain information against decay, and achieve cognitive goals. Distinct from cognitive load (the demand), effort quantifies the intensity of processing and directly influences the quality, speed, and sustainability of thought.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch32.S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter has defined the nature of this crucial resource and its immediate consequences. While the strategic allocation of effort (<math id="Ch32.S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>) shapes attention and executive control (the subject of the next chapter), understanding effort <math id="Ch32.S7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> itself is fundamental to appreciating the resource limitations and active nature of structured belief dynamics within <math id="Ch32.S7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It allows modeling the difference between passive processing and focused, deliberate cognitive work.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch32.S7.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Chapter Summary</h5>

<div id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter introduces Semantic Effort (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>), distinguishing it from Cognitive Load (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>). While load represents the demand on the system, effort represents the finite cognitive resources actively allocated and expended by the agent to perform operations within the semantic manifold <math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, constrained by a total capacity <math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>. Semantic effort is conceptualized as the quantifiable intensity of processing applied to tasks like assimilation (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>), reflection (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>), retrieval (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>), or coherence (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) maintenance. The chapter discusses how the level of exerted effort directly impacts cognitive performance, influencing processing quality and speed, counteracting belief decay via Nullification (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) by reinforcing anchors (<math id="Ch32.S7.SSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>), and potentially leading to resource depletion or fatigue if sustained at high levels. Although closely related (high load often necessitates high effort), effort (applied resource) and load (demand) are distinct. The strategic allocation of this effort, previewed for the next chapter, is central to attentional control. Effort is framed as the controllable "currency" of cognition.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch33" class="ltx_chapter">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 33 </span>Semantic Focus and Effort Allocation Policies</h3>

<section id="Ch33.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.1. </span>Introduction: Directing Cognitive Resources</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Chapter <a href="#Ch32" title="Chapter 32 Semantic Effort ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> introduced Semantic Effort (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) as the finite cognitive resource actively expended during processing within the semantic manifold <math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It defined the nature of this resource and its direct impact on the quality and sustainability of cognitive operations. However, possessing a resource is distinct from effectively directing it. Given limited total effort capacity <math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> and potentially numerous competing demands arising from external stimuli (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math>), internal dynamics (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t},K,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t},K,D</annotation></semantics></math>), retrieval (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>), reflection (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>), planning (<math id="Ch33.S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>), and simulation, how does an agent decide where to focus its cognitive exertion?</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch33.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter delves into the crucial mechanisms of semantic effort allocation and its relationship to attentional focus. We explore how an agent might implement control policies, denoted <math id="Ch33.S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>, to distribute its available effort <math id="Ch33.S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> across different processes, semantic sectors <math id="Ch33.S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, abstraction levels <math id="Ch33.S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, or specific belief fragments <math id="Ch33.S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We examine the inputs that inform these policies, the potential mechanisms by which allocated effort translates into focused processing (i.e., "attention"), various allocation strategies, and the possibility of learning effective policies over time (Chapter <a href="#Ch36" title="Chapter 36 Learning Regulatory Policies ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>). This provides the framework for understanding how agents achieve cognitive control, prioritize tasks, and concentrate their mental resources.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.2. </span>Formalizing Effort Allocation Policies (<math id="Ch33.S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{effort}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>effort</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{effort}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model effort allocation as a function or policy, <math id="Ch33.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented within the agent’s regulatory system (likely interacting closely with <math id="Ch33.S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math> and meta-cognitive monitoring).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch33.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 33.1 (Effort Allocation Policy <math id="Ch33.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span> An Effort Allocation Policy <math id="Ch33.S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the agent’s current state and context to a specific distribution of the available semantic effort <math id="Ch33.S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> across relevant cognitive targets:</p>
<table id="Ch33.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch33.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}:\Phi\times\text{Context}\rightarrow\text{Allocation}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Context</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>Allocation</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}:\Phi\times\text{Context}\rightarrow\text{Allocation}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch33.S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="Ch33.S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch33.S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> represents the current belief state (including meta-beliefs in <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Context includes factors like active goals, perceived environmental state, task demands.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Allocation specifies the distribution of effort, e.g., as a vector <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{1},\dots,\epsilon_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{1},\dots,\epsilon_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\epsilon_{i}\leq E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\epsilon_{i}\leq E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>. Targets <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> could be operators (e.g., <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{A},\epsilon_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{A},\epsilon_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>), sectors (e.g., <math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\Sigma_{plan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\Sigma_{plan}}</annotation></semantics></math>), specific beliefs (<math id="Ch33.S2.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\varphi_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\varphi_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>), or tasks.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch33.S2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The policy <math id="Ch33.S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> determines, moment-by-moment or strategically, how the agent invests its limited cognitive energy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.3. </span>Inputs Informing Allocation Policies</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Effective effort allocation requires integrating diverse information streams, primarily made available through Meta-Assimilation (<math id="Ch33.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, Chapter <a href="#Ch28" title="Chapter 28 Meta-Assimilation: Integrating Introspective Beliefs ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) into <math id="Ch33.S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="Ch33.S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Goals and Priorities:</span> Information from <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{plan}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{plan}</annotation></semantics></math> regarding active goals, subgoals, deadlines, and their relative importance heavily influences <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>. Higher priority goals receive greater <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cognitive Load (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Meta-beliefs about current load levels <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (Chapter <a href="#Ch31" title="Chapter 31 Cognitive Load ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) inform <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>. High load might trigger reallocation towards essential tasks or load-reduction strategies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coherence (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Detected incoherence (low <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) can trigger <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> to allocate resources towards corrective assimilation <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{corr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{corr}</annotation></semantics></math> or reflective analysis <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to restore consistency.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trajectory Awareness (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Meta-beliefs about trajectory properties (Chapter <a href="#Ch30" title="Chapter 30 Trajectory Awareness ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>), such as deviation from orientation axes (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>) or predicted entry into undesirable states, can guide <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> towards corrective steering or proactive replanning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Epistemic Identity (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The allocation policy <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> might be constrained by the need to maintain identity <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> (Chapter <a href="#Ch24" title="Chapter 24 Epistemic Identity ‣ Part VI Regulation and Control: Compass, Gauge, Identity ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), prioritizing effort towards reinforcing core beliefs or values when they are challenged.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">External Salience/Interrupts:</span> Salient external events processed via <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math> can trigger <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> to reallocate effort towards perceptual processing (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math>) and rapid response planning (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{plan}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{plan}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Available Capacity (<math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The policy must operate within the currently available resource limits, potentially scaling down allocations if fatigue reduces <math id="Ch33.S3.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch33.S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The sophistication of <math id="Ch33.S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the agent’s meta-cognitive capabilities to monitor these inputs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch33.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch33.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="200.64" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 402.68 200.64" width="402.68"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="translate(0,200.64) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(201.34,0) translate(0,109.54)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 37.77 19.69 L -37.77 19.69 C -40.83 19.69 -43.31 17.21 -43.31 14.15 L -43.31 -14.15 C -43.31 -17.21 -40.83 -19.69 -37.77 -19.69 L 37.77 -19.69 C 40.83 -19.69 43.31 -17.21 43.31 -14.15 L 43.31 14.15 C 43.31 17.21 40.83 19.69 37.77 19.69 Z M -43.31 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -35.74 -7.33)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.19)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.61em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="71.85"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effort Policy</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.43)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 19.14 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.59em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="33.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{effort}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">effort</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{effort}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -119.71 78.74 L -195.25 78.74 C -198.31 78.74 -200.79 76.26 -200.79 73.21 L -200.79 44.9 C -200.79 41.85 -198.31 39.37 -195.25 39.37 L -119.71 39.37 C -116.65 39.37 -114.17 41.85 -114.17 44.9 L -114.17 73.21 C -114.17 76.26 -116.65 78.74 -119.71 78.74 Z M -200.79 39.37"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -171.43 50.41)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 17.3)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.18em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="27.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Load</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.3)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 10.22 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="7.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -119.71 19.69 L -195.25 19.69 C -198.31 19.69 -200.79 17.21 -200.79 14.15 L -200.79 -14.15 C -200.79 -17.21 -198.31 -19.69 -195.25 -19.69 L -119.71 -19.69 C -116.65 -19.69 -114.17 -17.21 -114.17 -14.15 L -114.17 14.15 C -114.17 17.21 -116.65 19.69 -119.71 19.69 Z M -200.79 -19.69"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -195.22 -4.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.9em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="75.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Goal Salience</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -119.71 -39.37 L -195.25 -39.37 C -198.31 -39.37 -200.79 -41.85 -200.79 -44.9 L -200.79 -73.21 C -200.79 -76.26 -198.31 -78.74 -195.25 -78.74 L -119.71 -78.74 C -116.65 -78.74 -114.17 -76.26 -114.17 -73.21 L -114.17 -44.9 C -114.17 -41.85 -116.65 -39.37 -119.71 -39.37 Z M -200.79 -78.74"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -186.3 -66.06)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 14.01)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="57.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Coherence</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.01)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 25.13 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="5.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="7.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -113.62 42.6 L -49.44 18.52"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.93625 -0.35133 0.35133 0.93625 -52.41 19.63)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -113.62 0 L -49.82 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -52.99 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -113.62 -42.6 L -49.44 -18.52"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.93625 0.35133 -0.35133 0.93625 -52.41 -19.63)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 195.25 90.55 L 119.71 90.55 C 116.65 90.55 114.17 88.07 114.17 85.02 L 114.17 56.72 C 114.17 53.66 116.65 51.18 119.71 51.18 L 195.25 51.18 C 198.31 51.18 200.79 53.66 200.79 56.72 L 200.79 85.02 C 200.79 88.07 198.31 90.55 195.25 90.55 Z M 114.17 51.18"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 127.69 64.89)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 20.62)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="59.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Perception</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.29)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 16.92 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.34em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="25.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{perc}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">perc</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{perc}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 195.25 31.5 L 119.71 31.5 C 116.65 31.5 114.17 29.02 114.17 25.96 L 114.17 -2.34 C 114.17 -5.4 116.65 -7.87 119.71 -7.87 L 195.25 -7.87 C 198.31 -7.87 200.79 -5.4 200.79 -2.34 L 200.79 25.96 C 200.79 29.02 198.31 31.5 195.25 31.5 Z M 114.17 -7.87"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 132.5 5.76)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 20.76)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.9em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="49.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Planning</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.43)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 12.02 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.02em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.34em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="25.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{plan}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">plan</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{plan}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 195.25 -27.56 L 119.71 -27.56 C 116.65 -27.56 114.17 -30.04 114.17 -33.09 L 114.17 -61.39 C 114.17 -64.45 116.65 -66.93 119.71 -66.93 L 195.25 -66.93 C 198.31 -66.93 200.79 -64.45 200.79 -61.39 L 200.79 -33.09 C 200.79 -30.04 198.31 -27.56 195.25 -27.56 Z M 114.17 -66.93"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 129.48 -52.69)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 17.13)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="56.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reflection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.01)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 16.51 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{refl}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">refl</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\Sigma_{\text{refl}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 43.86 19.75 L 108.18 48.71"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.91182 0.41058 -0.41058 0.91182 105.29 47.41)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 43.86 3.29 L 107.68 8.08"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.9972 0.07484 -0.07484 0.9972 104.51 7.84)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 43.86 -13.16 L 107.91 -32.39"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.95776 -0.28754 0.28754 0.95776 104.87 -31.48)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -83.23 -101.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.21em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="79.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F1.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effort vector: <math id="Ch33.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{\Sigma_{1}},\ldots,\epsilon_{\Sigma_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\epsilon}=(\epsilon_{\Sigma_{1}},\ldots,\epsilon_{\Sigma_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch33.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 33.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch33.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effort allocation architecture. The policy <math id="Ch33.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{effort}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>effort</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{effort}}</annotation></semantics></math> receives introspective inputs—such as cognitive load <math id="Ch33.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, coherence <math id="Ch33.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, and goal salience—and produces an effort vector <math id="Ch33.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> distributing cognitive resources across semantic processes or sectors (e.g., perception, planning, reflection).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.4. </span>Mechanisms of Focus and Attention</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">How does allocating effort <math id="Ch33.S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to a specific target <math id="Ch33.S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., a belief <math id="Ch33.S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, sector <math id="Ch33.S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, operator <math id="Ch33.S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) translate into the functional phenomenon of "attentional focus"? Within the framework, several mechanisms could implement this:</p>
<ul id="Ch33.S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modulating Activation/Salience (<math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> Higher effort <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> directed towards <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> could directly boost its activation level <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\varphi_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\varphi_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\Sigma_{j},\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\Sigma_{j},\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>, making it more likely to influence subsequent processing (e.g., query generation <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, operator application).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prioritizing Operator Application:</span> <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> could bias the selection mechanism for applying operators (<math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,M,V,\Lambda,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,M,V,\Lambda,R</annotation></semantics></math>), preferentially applying them to belief fragments or sectors receiving high effort allocation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Differential Anchoring/Persistence:</span> Effort <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to maintain <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> could translate into a higher effective anchoring <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, slowing its decay under <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Attention actively preserves attended items in memory.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inhibition of Unattended Elements:</span> Allocating high effort <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> might concurrently trigger inhibitory signals that suppress the processing or activation (<math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) of unrelated beliefs or sectors, sharpening focus by reducing interference.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource-Gated Operator Performance:</span> The quality or speed of an operator <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>’s execution could directly depend on the effort <math id="Ch33.S4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{O}</annotation></semantics></math> allocated to it (as discussed in Chapter <a href="#Ch32" title="Chapter 32 Semantic Effort ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>). Attention enables deeper processing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Ch33.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch33.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="252.46" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 413.81 252.46" width="413.81"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,252.46) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(55.67,0) translate(0,160.25)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 46.82 23.62 L -46.82 23.62 C -51.4 23.62 -55.12 19.91 -55.12 15.32 L -55.12 -15.32 C -55.12 -19.91 -51.4 -23.62 -46.82 -23.62 L 46.82 -23.62 C 51.4 -23.62 55.12 -19.91 55.12 -15.32 L 55.12 15.32 C 55.12 19.91 51.4 23.62 46.82 23.62 Z M -55.12 -23.62"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -47.39 -6.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 20.34)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="94.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effort Allocation</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.16)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 13.68 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="68.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to Target</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 339.26 23.62 L 245.63 23.62 C 241.04 23.62 237.33 19.91 237.33 15.32 L 237.33 -15.32 C 237.33 -19.91 241.04 -23.62 245.63 -23.62 L 339.26 -23.62 C 343.85 -23.62 347.56 -19.91 347.56 -15.32 L 347.56 15.32 C 347.56 19.91 343.85 23.62 339.26 23.62 Z M 237.33 -23.62"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 245.04 -7.33)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 21.03)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="95.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Boost Activation</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.85)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 31.69 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.52" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="31.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\varphi_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\varphi_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 342.33 91.66 L 242.56 91.66 C 237.98 91.66 234.26 87.94 234.26 83.36 L 234.26 52.72 C 234.26 48.13 237.98 44.41 242.56 44.41 L 342.33 44.41 C 346.92 44.41 350.63 48.13 350.63 52.72 L 350.63 83.36 C 350.63 87.94 346.92 91.66 342.33 91.66 Z M 234.26 44.41"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 238.87 61.41)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 19.61)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="107.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Increase Anchoring</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 16.43)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 47.36 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.54" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="12.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch33.F2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 342.41 -44.41 L 242.48 -44.41 C 237.89 -44.41 234.18 -48.13 234.18 -52.72 L 234.18 -83.36 C 234.18 -87.94 237.89 -91.66 242.48 -91.66 L 342.41 -91.66 C 347 -91.66 350.72 -87.94 350.72 -83.36 L 350.72 -52.72 C 350.72 -48.13 347 -44.41 342.41 -44.41 Z M 234.18 -91.66"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 238.79 -76.61)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 22)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="106.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prioritize Operator</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 19.58)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 21.13 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.08em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="65.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Application</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 349.28 -112.45 L 235.61 -112.45 C 231.03 -112.45 227.31 -116.17 227.31 -120.75 L 227.31 -151.39 C 227.31 -155.98 231.03 -159.69 235.61 -159.69 L 349.28 -159.69 C 353.86 -159.69 357.58 -155.98 357.58 -151.39 L 357.58 -120.75 C 357.58 -116.17 353.86 -112.45 349.28 -112.45 Z M 227.31 -159.69"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 231.92 -139.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="121.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch33.F2.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Suppress Distractions</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 55.67 0 L 126.54 0"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 126.54 0 L 126.54 0 L 230.81 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 227.64 0)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 126.54 0 L 126.54 68.04 L 227.74 68.04"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 224.57 68.04)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 126.54 0 L 126.54 -68.04 L 227.66 -68.04"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 224.49 -68.04)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 126.54 0 L 126.54 -136.07 L 220.79 -136.07"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 217.62 -136.07)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch33.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 33.2</span>. </span><span id="Ch33.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mechanisms of focus. Semantic effort <math id="Ch33.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> allocated to a target (belief fragment <math id="Ch33.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, sector <math id="Ch33.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, or operator <math id="Ch33.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) influences cognitive processing through multiple pathways: boosting activation <math id="Ch33.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, increasing anchoring <math id="Ch33.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, prioritizing operator application, and inhibiting unrelated elements. Focus emerges from structured modulation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch33.S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Attention/focus, in this view, is not a separate module but an emergent consequence of how the allocation policy <math id="Ch33.S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> directs the finite resource <math id="Ch33.S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to modulate the activation and processing priorities within the semantic manifold <math id="Ch33.S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S5" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.5. </span>Effort Allocation Strategies</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The policy <math id="Ch33.S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> can implement various high-level strategies for managing cognitive resources, selected based on the inputs described in Section 3:</p>
<ul id="Ch33.S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Goal Shielding:</span> When a high-priority goal is active (input from <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{plan}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{plan}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> allocates maximal effort <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to processes directly supporting that goal (e.g., planning in <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{plan}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{plan}</annotation></semantics></math>, relevant retrieval <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, necessary simulation) while actively inhibiting or allocating minimal effort to potentially distracting inputs or unrelated reflective processes (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl},\Sigma_{narr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl},\Sigma_{narr}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Load Balancing:</span> If meta-cognition (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>) reports high overall load <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> or high load in a specific sector (e.g., <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\Sigma_{perc},\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\Sigma_{perc},\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is excessive), <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> might reduce effort allocated to non-critical background tasks and/or allocate effort specifically to load-reducing actions like Abstraction (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) or targeted Nullification (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vigilance/Monitoring:</span> In stable or low-demand situations, <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> might adopt a vigilance strategy, allocating a baseline level of effort to perceptual monitoring (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{perc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{perc}</annotation></semantics></math>) and routine coherence checking (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) to ensure readiness for unexpected events or gradual drift.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exploration vs. Exploitation:</span> Depending on task phase or uncertainty levels (assessed via <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> could shift allocation. High uncertainty might trigger allocation towards exploring new information (effort <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for novel input <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math>), while consolidating understanding might trigger effort allocation towards internal reflection (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>) or re-anchoring important memories (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\rightarrow R\rightarrow A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\rightarrow R\rightarrow A</annotation></semantics></math> cycles).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reactive vs. Deliberative Allocation:</span> Under severe time pressure or detected crisis (input from Context or <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> might default to a reactive strategy, allocating effort primarily based on immediate external salience (<math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)</annotation></semantics></math>) or simple triggers. In less pressured situations, it might allocate significant effort <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to meta-cognitive deliberation within <math id="Ch33.S5.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine a more optimal long-term effort distribution before committing resources.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch33.S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The choice of strategy might itself be context-dependent or learned (Chapter <a href="#Ch36" title="Chapter 36 Learning Regulatory Policies ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.6. </span>Learning Effective Allocation Policies</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optimal allocation of semantic effort is unlikely to be fixed; agents should learn effective <math id="Ch33.S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> policies. Potential learning mechanisms include:</p>
<ul id="Ch33.S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reinforcement Learning:</span> Using task success, goal achievement, or internal metrics (e.g., maintaining high <math id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, low unexpected trajectory deviation <math id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>) as rewards to train <math id="Ch33.S6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Imitation Learning:</span> Learning allocation strategies by observing demonstrators (human or other AI).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Meta-Learning:</span> Adapting the parameters of <math id="Ch33.S6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> itself based on performance across different types of tasks or contexts (learning how to allocate effort differently in different situations).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch33.S6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch33.S6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch33.S6.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evolutionary Methods:</span> Selecting effective allocation strategies over generations in simulated populations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch33.S6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Learning efficient resource management policies is crucial for scaling cognitive capabilities and achieving robust performance in complex environments, as detailed further in Chapter <a href="#Ch36" title="Chapter 36 Learning Regulatory Policies ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch33.S7" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">33.7. </span>Conclusion: Attention as Controlled Effort</h4>

<div id="Ch33.S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic focus and attentional control emerge within this framework not as separate modules, but as consequences of the agent’s ability to strategically allocate its finite semantic effort (<math id="Ch33.S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>). The allocation policy, <math id="Ch33.S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>, acts as the central executive, directing resources based on meta-cognitive assessments of goals, load, coherence, trajectory, and identity.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch33.S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By formalizing <math id="Ch33.S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math> and its potential mechanisms (modulating activation <math id="Ch33.S7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, prioritizing operators, inhibiting distractions), we gain a principled way to model attentional phenomena and resource management within the semantic manifold <math id="Ch33.S7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. This chapter, complementing the previous one on the nature of effort <math id="Ch33.S7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, provides the control layer necessary for understanding how agents focus their cognitive energy, manage trade-offs, and ultimately direct their own thought processes. Effective effort allocation, guided by sophisticated meta-cognition, is key to flexible, efficient, and goal-directed reasoning in any resource-constrained intelligent system.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch33.S7.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Chapter Summary</h5>

<div id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter addresses how the finite cognitive resource of Semantic Effort (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, introduced in Chapter <a href="#Ch32" title="Chapter 32 Semantic Effort ‣ Part VIII Meta-Cognition and Recursive Regulation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) is directed and managed, linking its allocation to the concepts of semantic focus and attention. It introduces Effort Allocation Policies (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{effort}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{effort}</annotation></semantics></math>) as the control mechanisms responsible for distributing the available effort capacity (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>) across various cognitive processes, semantic sectors (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>), abstraction levels (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>), or specific belief fragments within <math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>. These policies are informed by diverse inputs, including active goals, current cognitive load (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), coherence levels (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>), trajectory awareness, and contextual demands, often synthesized through meta-cognitive processing (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>) in <math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{refl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{refl}</annotation></semantics></math>. The chapter discusses how allocated effort translates into functional focus, potentially through mechanisms like modulating belief activation (<math id="Ch33.S7.SSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), prioritizing operator applications, inhibiting unattended elements, or gating processing quality. Various allocation strategies, such as goal shielding, load balancing, and vigilance, are outlined. Ultimately, attention and focus are presented not as separate modules but as emergent outcomes of the agent’s learned or designed policies for controlling its limited cognitive energy.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt9" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_part">Part IX </span>Learning and Adaptation</h2>

<section id="Ch34" class="ltx_chapter">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 34 </span>Learning Semantic Structures</h3>

<section id="Ch34.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">34.1. </span>Introduction: The Plasticity of Mind-Space</h4>

<div id="Ch34.S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding Parts of this monograph have detailed a rich architecture for structured belief, defined by the semantic state space <math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> (parameterized by <math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>), its internal structuring via semantic scaling (<math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>) and sectors (<math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>), and its geometry characterized conceptually by a semantic metric (<math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>). While we have discussed the dynamics (<math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,M,N_{t},K,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,M,N_{t},K,\dots</annotation></semantics></math>) operating within this space and the regulatory mechanisms controlling trajectories (<math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>), we have largely treated the underlying structure itself as given or predefined by the agent’s design <math id="Ch34.S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch34.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, a truly adaptive and intelligent system, especially one aiming for human-like flexibility, likely requires its internal representational structures to be plastic—shaped and refined by experience and learning. How might the very fabric of the semantic manifold <math id="Ch34.S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, its geometry, and its functional organization into sectors <math id="Ch34.S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> arise or adapt over time?</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch34.S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter initiates our exploration of learning within the Semantic Manifold framework (Part <a href="#Pt9" title="Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a>) by focusing on the acquisition and adaptation of its foundational structures. We consider potential mechanisms by which the semantic metric <math id="Ch34.S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> could be learned, how functional sectors <math id="Ch34.S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> might emerge or differentiate, and speculate on the adaptability of the manifold’s geometry itself. <span id="Ch34.S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The objective of such structural learning is to optimize the representational space itself for better performance, efficiency, or coherence in the agent’s cognitive tasks.</span> This focus on structural learning complements the subsequent chapters which will address the learning of cognitive operators (Chapter <a href="#Ch35" title="Chapter 35 Learning Cognitive Operators ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) and regulatory policies (Chapter <a href="#Ch36" title="Chapter 36 Learning Regulatory Policies ‣ Part IX Learning and Adaptation ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch34.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">34.2. </span>Learning the Semantic Metric (<math id="Ch34.S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="Ch34.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The semantic metric <math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> plays a fundamental role, underpinning similarity judgments, retrieval (<math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>), coherence evaluation (<math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>), orientation (<math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>), and potentially operator application (<math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,M,\Lambda,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,M,\Lambda,V</annotation></semantics></math>). A predefined, static metric may fail to capture the nuanced, context-dependent, and evolving nature of semantic similarity required for sophisticated cognition. Therefore, mechanisms for learning or adapting <math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> are highly desirable. <span id="Ch34.S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The primary objective for learning <math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is to ensure that distances in <math id="Ch34.S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> accurately reflect functional or semantic similarity relevant to the agent’s tasks and goals,</span> leading to improved retrieval, coherence assessment, and generalization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch34.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch34.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="260.95" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 190.08 260.95" width="190.08"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,260.95) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(16.3,0) translate(0,189.53)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 15.75 19.69 C 15.75 28.38 8.7 35.43 0 35.43 C -8.7 35.43 -15.75 28.38 -15.75 19.69 C -15.75 10.99 -8.7 3.94 0 3.94 C 8.7 3.94 15.75 10.99 15.75 19.69 Z M 0 19.69"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -7.19 18.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 78.74 55.12 C 78.74 63.82 71.69 70.87 62.99 70.87 C 54.29 70.87 47.24 63.82 47.24 55.12 C 47.24 46.42 54.29 39.37 62.99 39.37 C 71.69 39.37 78.74 46.42 78.74 55.12 Z M 62.99 55.12"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 55.8 53.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 66.93 0 C 66.93 8.7 59.88 15.75 51.18 15.75 C 42.48 15.75 35.43 8.7 35.43 0 C 35.43 -8.7 42.48 -15.75 51.18 -15.75 C 59.88 -15.75 66.93 -8.7 66.93 0 Z M 51.18 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 43.99 -1.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 118.11 15.75 C 118.11 24.45 111.06 31.5 102.36 31.5 C 93.66 31.5 86.61 24.45 86.61 15.75 C 86.61 7.05 93.66 -0 102.36 -0 C 111.06 -0 118.11 7.05 118.11 15.75 Z M 102.36 15.75"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 95.17 14.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 157.48 39.37 C 157.48 48.07 150.43 55.12 141.73 55.12 C 133.04 55.12 125.98 48.07 125.98 39.37 C 125.98 30.67 133.04 23.62 141.73 23.62 C 150.43 23.62 157.48 30.67 157.48 39.37 Z M 141.73 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 134.54 37.9)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{5}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path d="M 150.98 -56.23 L 30.12 -56.23 C 25.54 -56.23 21.82 -59.94 21.82 -64.53 L 21.82 -87.29 C 21.82 -91.88 25.54 -95.6 30.12 -95.6 L 150.98 -95.6 C 155.57 -95.6 159.28 -91.88 159.28 -87.29 L 159.28 -64.53 C 159.28 -59.94 155.57 -56.23 150.98 -56.23 Z M 21.82 -95.6"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 26.43 -83.24)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 21.03)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.05em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="128.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch34.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Learn Semantic Metric</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.85)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 39.51 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.52" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="49.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\varphi_{i},\varphi_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\varphi_{i},\varphi_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 3.38 L 85.56 -52.42"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.83762 -0.54626 0.54626 0.83762 82.9 -50.68)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 62.99 38.82 L 88.88 -49.95"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.28 -0.96 0.96 0.28 87.99 -46.9)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 51.18 -16.3 L 86.34 -51.46"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.7071 -0.7071 0.7071 0.7071 84.09 -49.21)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 102.36 -0.55 L 91.8 -49.84"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.20953 -0.9778 0.9778 -0.20953 92.46 -46.74)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 141.73 23.07 L 93.8 -50.67"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.54498 -0.83844 0.83844 -0.54498 95.53 -48.01)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 35.43 -165.35 C 35.43 -156.66 28.38 -149.61 19.69 -149.61 C 10.99 -149.61 3.94 -156.66 3.94 -165.35 C 3.94 -174.05 10.99 -181.1 19.69 -181.1 C 28.38 -181.1 35.43 -174.05 35.43 -165.35 Z M 19.69 -165.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 -166.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 70.87 -141.73 C 70.87 -133.04 63.82 -125.98 55.12 -125.98 C 46.42 -125.98 39.37 -133.04 39.37 -141.73 C 39.37 -150.43 46.42 -157.48 55.12 -157.48 C 63.82 -157.48 70.87 -150.43 70.87 -141.73 Z M 55.12 -141.73"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 47.93 -143.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 94.49 -173.23 C 94.49 -164.53 87.44 -157.48 78.74 -157.48 C 70.04 -157.48 62.99 -164.53 62.99 -173.23 C 62.99 -181.93 70.04 -188.98 78.74 -188.98 C 87.44 -188.98 94.49 -181.93 94.49 -173.23 Z M 78.74 -173.23"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 71.55 -174.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 133.86 -149.61 C 133.86 -140.91 126.81 -133.86 118.11 -133.86 C 109.41 -133.86 102.36 -140.91 102.36 -149.61 C 102.36 -158.3 109.41 -165.35 118.11 -165.35 C 126.81 -165.35 133.86 -158.3 133.86 -149.61 Z M 118.11 -149.61"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 110.92 -151.08)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.23 -165.35 C 173.23 -156.66 166.18 -149.61 157.48 -149.61 C 148.78 -149.61 141.73 -156.66 141.73 -165.35 C 141.73 -174.05 148.78 -181.1 157.48 -181.1 C 166.18 -181.1 173.23 -174.05 173.23 -165.35 Z M 157.48 -165.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 150.29 -166.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.42em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="7.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.36)" width="14.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">φ</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{5}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 90.55 -96.15 L 90.55 -120.02"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 90.55 -116.85)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 33.25 -156.31 L 41.55 -150.78"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 64.9 -154.77 L 68.96 -160.19"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 92.72 -164.84 L 104.13 -157.99"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 133.25 -155.66 L 142.34 -159.3"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch34.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 34.1</span>. </span><span id="Ch34.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Learning semantic distance. Raw belief fragments <math id="Ch34.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are processed through metric learning (<math id="Ch34.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>), resulting in a structured space where distances reflect semantic similarity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch34.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ch34.S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dependence on Representation (<math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> The methods for learning <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> are intrinsically tied to the chosen representation mode <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (parameter in <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, Chapter <a href="#Ch8" title="Chapter 8 Parameterized Semantic Architectures ‣ Part II Semantic Foundations: The Semantic Substrate ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning in Embedding Spaces (<math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx</annotation></semantics></math> Embedding):</span> If beliefs are represented as vectors, <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> might be related to standard vector space metrics (Euclidean, Cosine). Learning <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> then becomes equivalent to learning effective embedding functions. Techniques include:</p>
<ul id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contrastive Learning:</span> Training embedding models (e.g., variants of BERT, Sentence-BERT, or custom networks) to pull semantically related belief fragments <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varphi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varphi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> closer together in the embedding space while pushing unrelated ones apart, based on supervision derived from co-occurrence, entailment relations, or task performance rewards that signal semantic similarity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric Learning:</span> Directly learning a parameterized distance function <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\psi}(v_{1},v_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\psi}(v_{1},v_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> over a base embedding space, where parameters <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> are optimized to satisfy desired similarity constraints derived from experience or task feedback.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning in Symbolic/Graph Spaces (<math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx</annotation></semantics></math> Symbolic/Graph):</span> For symbolic or graph representations, learning <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> might involve:</p>
<ul id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Learning weights on structural features or links used in distance calculation (e.g., weighted edit distance, learned graph similarity kernels), optimizing weights to reflect functional similarity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Learning structural alignment algorithms that best capture semantic relatedness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Influence of Grounding:</span> The learning process for <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> should ideally be informed by grounding (Chapter <a href="#Ch9" title="Chapter 9 Grounding Semantic Belief ‣ Part III Structuring Belief: Modularity and Abstraction ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Beliefs grounded in similar sensorimotor experiences or linguistic contexts should map to points closer in <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> according to the learned <math id="Ch34.S2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ch34.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">An adaptive semantic metric <math id="Ch34.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> allows the agent’s notion of similarity to evolve, reflecting its growing knowledge and experience, ultimately improving the foundation for many cognitive operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch34.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">34.3. </span>Emergence and Refinement of Semantic Sectors (<math id="Ch34.S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="Ch34.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic sectors <math id="Ch34.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> provide functional modularity within <math id="Ch34.S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, partitioning beliefs based on their role (e.g., <math id="Ch34.S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{perc},\Sigma_{plan},\Sigma_{refl},\Sigma_{narr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{perc},\Sigma_{plan},\Sigma_{refl},\Sigma_{narr}</annotation></semantics></math>). While Chapter <a href="#Ch11" title="Chapter 11 Semantic Sectors ‣ Part III Structuring Belief: Modularity and Abstraction ‣ Theoretical Foundations for Semantic Cognition in Artificial Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> suggested these might be somewhat predefined structurally, a more powerful model allows them to emerge or be refined through learning. <span id="Ch34.S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The objective here is to develop a sectoral organization that optimally supports modular processing, reduces interference between functional subsystems, and facilitates efficient task execution.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch34.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Ch34.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="168.87" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 547.03 168.87" width="547.03"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,168.87) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(255.14,0) translate(0,0.55)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -250.52 154.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.3em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10.65pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="225.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch34.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Initial Belief Space (Unstructured)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -155.52 78.74 C -155.52 79.82 -156.4 80.7 -157.48 80.7 C -158.56 80.7 -159.44 79.82 -159.44 78.74 C -159.44 77.66 -158.56 76.78 -157.48 76.78 C -156.4 76.78 -155.52 77.66 -155.52 78.74 Z M -157.48 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -135.84 59.06 C -135.84 60.14 -136.71 61.01 -137.8 61.01 C -138.88 61.01 -139.75 60.14 -139.75 59.06 C -139.75 57.97 -138.88 57.1 -137.8 57.1 C -136.71 57.1 -135.84 57.97 -135.84 59.06 Z M -137.8 59.06"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -108.28 86.61 C -108.28 87.69 -109.16 88.57 -110.24 88.57 C -111.32 88.57 -112.19 87.69 -112.19 86.61 C -112.19 85.53 -111.32 84.66 -110.24 84.66 C -109.16 84.66 -108.28 85.53 -108.28 86.61 Z M -110.24 86.61"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -124.03 39.37 C -124.03 40.45 -124.9 41.33 -125.98 41.33 C -127.06 41.33 -127.94 40.45 -127.94 39.37 C -127.94 38.29 -127.06 37.41 -125.98 37.41 C -124.9 37.41 -124.03 38.29 -124.03 39.37 Z M -125.98 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -163.4 47.24 C -163.4 48.32 -164.27 49.2 -165.35 49.2 C -166.44 49.2 -167.31 48.32 -167.31 47.24 C -167.31 46.16 -166.44 45.29 -165.35 45.29 C -164.27 45.29 -163.4 46.16 -163.4 47.24 Z M -165.35 47.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M -116.15 102.36 C -116.15 103.44 -117.03 104.32 -118.11 104.32 C -119.19 104.32 -120.07 103.44 -120.07 102.36 C -120.07 101.28 -119.19 100.41 -118.11 100.41 C -117.03 100.41 -116.15 101.28 -116.15 102.36 Z M -118.11 102.36"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -90.55 70.87 L 13.72 70.87"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.55 70.87)"><path d="M 7.66 0 L 1.79 2.18 L 3.45 0 L 1.79 -2.18 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -88.55 78.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="105.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch34.F2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Learning Processes</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 56.03 154.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10.65pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="194.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Ch34.F2.pic1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Emergent Semantic Sectors (<math id="Ch34.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 133.86 78.74 C 133.86 100.48 109.18 118.11 78.74 118.11 C 48.3 118.11 23.62 100.48 23.62 78.74 C 23.62 57 48.3 39.37 78.74 39.37 C 109.18 39.37 133.86 57 133.86 78.74 Z M 78.74 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 63.83 126.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="29.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{perc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">perc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{perc}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 212.6 39.37 C 212.6 61.11 187.92 78.74 157.48 78.74 C 127.04 78.74 102.36 61.11 102.36 39.37 C 102.36 17.63 127.04 0 157.48 0 C 187.92 0 212.6 17.63 212.6 39.37 Z M 157.48 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 142.42 87.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.27em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="11.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="30.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{plan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">plan</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{plan}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 291.34 78.74 C 291.34 100.48 266.66 118.11 236.22 118.11 C 205.78 118.11 181.1 100.48 181.1 78.74 C 181.1 57 205.78 39.37 236.22 39.37 C 266.66 39.37 291.34 57 291.34 78.74 Z M 236.22 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 223.56 125.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="25.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="Ch34.F2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{refl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">refl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{refl}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 68.89 86.61 C 68.89 87.69 68.01 88.57 66.93 88.57 C 65.85 88.57 64.97 87.69 64.97 86.61 C 64.97 85.53 65.85 84.66 66.93 84.66 C 68.01 84.66 68.89 85.53 68.89 86.61 Z M 66.93 86.61"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 88.57 70.87 C 88.57 71.95 87.69 72.82 86.61 72.82 C 85.53 72.82 84.66 71.95 84.66 70.87 C 84.66 69.79 85.53 68.91 86.61 68.91 C 87.69 68.91 88.57 69.79 88.57 70.87 Z M 86.61 70.87"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 92.51 94.49 C 92.51 95.57 91.63 96.44 90.55 96.44 C 89.47 96.44 88.59 95.57 88.59 94.49 C 88.59 93.41 89.47 92.53 90.55 92.53 C 91.63 92.53 92.51 93.41 92.51 94.49 Z M 90.55 94.49"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 147.63 47.24 C 147.63 48.32 146.75 49.2 145.67 49.2 C 144.59 49.2 143.71 48.32 143.71 47.24 C 143.71 46.16 144.59 45.29 145.67 45.29 C 146.75 45.29 147.63 46.16 147.63 47.24 Z M 145.67 47.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 171.25 31.5 C 171.25 32.58 170.37 33.45 169.29 33.45 C 168.21 33.45 167.33 32.58 167.33 31.5 C 167.33 30.42 168.21 29.54 169.29 29.54 C 170.37 29.54 171.25 30.42 171.25 31.5 Z M 169.29 31.5"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 159.44 59.06 C 159.44 60.14 158.56 61.01 157.48 61.01 C 156.4 61.01 155.52 60.14 155.52 59.06 C 155.52 57.97 156.4 57.1 157.48 57.1 C 158.56 57.1 159.44 57.97 159.44 59.06 Z M 157.48 59.06"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 226.37 86.61 C 226.37 87.69 225.49 88.57 224.41 88.57 C 223.33 88.57 222.45 87.69 222.45 86.61 C 222.45 85.53 223.33 84.66 224.41 84.66 C 225.49 84.66 226.37 85.53 226.37 86.61 Z M 224.41 86.61"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 246.05 78.74 C 246.05 79.82 245.18 80.7 244.09 80.7 C 243.01 80.7 242.14 79.82 242.14 78.74 C 242.14 77.66 243.01 76.78 244.09 76.78 C 245.18 76.78 246.05 77.66 246.05 78.74 Z M 244.09 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 249.99 98.43 C 249.99 99.51 249.11 100.38 248.03 100.38 C 246.95 100.38 246.07 99.51 246.07 98.43 C 246.07 97.34 246.95 96.47 248.03 96.47 C 249.11 96.47 249.99 97.34 249.99 98.43 Z M 248.03 98.43"></path></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch34.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 34.2</span>. </span><span id="Ch34.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Emergence of Semantic Sectors through Learning. Initially, the belief space <math id="Ch34.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is unstructured. Learning processes, such as activity correlation and clustering, drive the differentiation of <math id="Ch34.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> into functional sectors like perception (<math id="Ch34.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{perc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>perc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{perc}}</annotation></semantics></math>), planning (<math id="Ch34.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{plan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>plan</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{plan}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and reflection (<math id="Ch34.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{refl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>refl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{refl}}</annotation></semantics></math>), facilitating modular cognitive processing.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch34.S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ch34.S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch34.S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activity Correlation / Hebbian Learning:</span> Sectors might emerge from patterns of co-activation. Belief fragments <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varphi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varphi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that are frequently processed together (e.g., involved in planning sequences, or part of reflective loops) could become strongly interconnected, forming functional clusters that differentiate into sectors over time.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clustering Methods:</span> Unsupervised or semi-supervised clustering algorithms applied to the belief space <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> (based on the learned metric <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and connectivity) could identify natural groupings corresponding to functional sectors, aiming to maximize intra-sector coherence and minimize inter-sector dependencies where appropriate.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task-Driven Specialization:</span> If the agent learns different tasks, reinforcement learning or supervised learning might drive the specialization of different parts of <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> (or underlying neural substrates if implemented that way) to handle specific task-related functions, leading to the emergence of <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> that optimize task performance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modular Training:</span> Explicitly training distinct modules (e.g., separate neural networks) for different functions (perception, planning, reflection) and composing them could instantiate a structured <math id="Ch34.S3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> with predefined but potentially adaptable sectors, where adaptation optimizes the interfaces or specialization of modules.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Ch34.S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The ability to learn or refine sectoral organization allows the agent to develop specialized processing pathways tailored to its cognitive needs and experiences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch34.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">34.4. </span>Adapting Manifold Geometry (Speculative)</h4>

<div id="Ch34.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond learning the metric <math id="Ch34.S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> or the sectoral organization <math id="Ch34.S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, could the fundamental geometric or topological structure of <math id="Ch34.S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> itself adapt through learning? This is more speculative but theoretically interesting. <span id="Ch34.S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The potential objective would be to find a geometry that most efficiently or robustly represents the semantic relationships relevant to the agent’s world and tasks.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ch34.S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ch34.S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dimensionality Reduction/Expansion:</span> Learning processes (like those used for <math id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) might implicitly learn an appropriate intrinsic dimensionality for representing beliefs within <math id="Ch34.S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, potentially changing over time or across sectors to balance representational richness and computational cost.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning Curvature/Topology:</span> Could the agent learn that certain regions of semantic space exhibit higher "curvature" (representing ambiguity or complex interactions) and adapt its processing accordingly? Could topological features (holes, boundaries) emerge reflecting conceptual distinctions learned from data?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch34.S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch34.S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch34.S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch34.S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Challenges:</span> Formalizing and implementing mechanisms for learning the underlying manifold geometry itself is significantly harder than learning a metric or clustering on a predefined space. This remains a challenging research direction, potentially involving advanced concepts from geometric deep learning or topological data analysis. Defining clear learning objectives and stable algorithms for such adaptation is difficult.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
